# L §4.6 step 3.2 (round 11b): "of two rows neither of which is narrower (... or `[a, *]` and `[*, b]`), neither
# wins here"; one version, both always: step 4, LOAD-OVERLAP at load.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

index ns = 1..10
index ms = 1..3
input x[n in ns, k in ms]: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  x[2, *] = 2
  x[*, 3] = 1

ask q: x[2, 3]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-OVERLAP ...
